@@ -8,6 +8,10 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- **Tool inputs are validated against each tool's declared `inputSchema` before the executor runs.** `ToolRegistry.register` now compiles static schemas up front and throws synchronously naming the tool when a schema is invalid; function-valued tool definitions resolve and cache compiled validators per returned schema object. When a model call fails `required`, declared property types or `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` logs and returns a `ToolResponse` naming only the failing field paths and constraints — never offending values — instead of invoking the executor or throwing, so the model can correct the call on the next tool round. Extra properties not listed in the schema still pass through unchanged, with no type coercion or default injection. **Migration:** executors that previously hand-validated their input now receive only payloads their `inputSchema` accepts, and any tool that relied on receiving malformed input to format its own error message will no longer be called for schema-rejected inputs.
+
